{"id":"mahabharata-7-149","work":"mahabharata","part":7,"partName":"द्रोणपर्व","partNameEn":"Drona Parva","unit":149,"title":"एकोनपञ्चाशदधिकशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 149 · Ghatotkacha drives back the Kauravas","summary":{"en":"Ghatotkacha rushes at Karna and routs the Kaurava troops, who flee through the night. The two masters of illusion try to outdo each other and the fight grows marvellous and terrible.","kn":"ಘಟೋತ್ಕಚ ಕರ್ಣನ ಮೇಲೆ ಎರಗಿ ಕೌರವ ಸೈನ್ಯವನ್ನು ಓಡಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಅವರು ರಾತ್ರಿಯಲ್ಲಿ ಚದುರುತ್ತಾರೆ. ಮಾಯೆಯಲ್ಲಿ ನಿಪುಣರಾದ ಇಬ್ಬರೂ ಒಬ್ಬರನ್ನೊಬ್ಬರು ಮೀರಲು ಯತ್ನಿಸುತ್ತಾರೆ; ಯುದ್ಧ ಅದ್ಭುತ, ಭಯಂಕರವಾಗುತ್ತದೆ.","hi":"घटोत्कच कर्ण पर झपटकर कौरव सेना को भगाता है जो रात में तितर-बितर हो जाती है। मायावी दोनों एक-दूसरे को मात देने का प्रयत्न करते हैं और युद्ध अद्भुत और भयंकर हो जाता है।","te":"ఘటోత్కచుడు కర్ణునిపై దూకి కౌరవ సేనను తరుముతాడు; వారు రాత్రిలో చెదిరిపోతారు. మాయలో నిపుణులైన ఇద్దరూ ఒకరినొకరు మించాలని ప్రయత్నిస్తారు; యుద్ధం అద్భుతంగా, భయంకరంగా మారుతుంది.","ta":"கடோத்கசன் கர்ணனைத் தாக்கிக் கௌரவப் படையை விரட்ட, அவர்கள் இரவில் சிதறுகின்றனர். மாயையில் வல்ல இருவரும் ஒருவரை ஒருவர் மிஞ்ச முயல, போர் அற்புதமாகவும் கொடிதாகவும் ஆகிறது.","ml":"ഘടോൽക്കചൻ കർണ്ണന്റെ നേർക്ക് പാഞ്ഞടുത്ത് കൗരവ സേനയെ തോൽപ്പിക്കുന്നു; അവർ രാത്രിയിലൂടെ ഓടിപ്പോകുന്നു. മായാവിദ്യയുടെ രണ്ട് യജമാനന്മാർ പരസ്പരം മറികടക്കാൻ ശ്രമിക്കുന്നു; യുദ്ധം അത്ഭുതകരവും ഭയങ്കരവുമായി മാറുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 7.149; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Sep 22 2026","sections":[{"title":"घटोत्कचवधपर्व","titleEn":"Ghatotkachavadha Parva (Slaying of Ghatotkacha)","verses":[{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"दृष्ट्वा घटोत्कचं राजन्सूतपुत्ररथं प्रति ।\nप्रयान्तं त्वरया युक्तं जिघांसुं कर्णमाहवे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing Ghatotkacha hurrying toward the charioteer's son's chariot, wishing to kill Karna in battle, O king,"}},{"n":2,"text":"अब्रवीत्तव पुत्रस्तु दुःशासनमिदं वचः ।\nएतद्रक्षो रणे तूर्णं दृष्ट्वा कर्णस्य विक्रमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"your son said this to Dushasana: \"That rakshasa, having seen Karna's prowess in battle, is quickly attacking Karna."}},{"n":3,"text":"अभियाति द्रुतं कर्णं तद्वारय महारथम् ।\nवृतः सैन्येन महता याहि यत्र महाबलः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Stop him, great warrior. Go with a big army to where he, the mighty one, is."}},{"n":4,"text":"कर्णो वैकर्तनो युद्धे राक्षसेन युयुत्सति ।\nरक्ष कर्णं रणे यत्तो वृतः सैन्येन मानद ॥","meaning":{"en":"Karna, Vikartana's son, wants to fight the rakshasa. Guard Karna in the battle, vigilant and with the army around you, honored one.\""}},{"n":5,"text":"एतस्मिन्नन्तरे राजञ्जटासुरसुतो बली ।\nदुर्योधनमुपागम्य प्राह प्रहरतां वरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"In the meantime, O king, the strong son of Jatasura (Alambala), best of strikers, came to Duryodhana and said:"}},{"n":6,"text":"दुर्योधन तवामित्रान्प्रख्यातान्युद्धदुर्मदान् ।\nपाण्डवान्हन्तुमिच्छामि त्वयाज्ञप्तः सहानुगान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Duryodhana, I want to kill, at your command, your famous enemies, the Pandavas, fierce in battle, with their followers."}},{"n":7,"text":"जटासुरो मम पिता रक्षसामग्रणीः पुरा ।\nप्रयुज्य कर्म रक्षोघ्नं क्षुद्रैः पार्थैर्निपातितः ।\nतस्यापचितिमिच्छामि त्वद्दिष्टो गन्तुमीश्वर ॥","meaning":{"en":"Jatasura was my father, once the foremost of rakshasas; he was killed by the petty Parthas after he tried a rakshasa-destroying rite. I want to avenge him; let me go, lord, directed by you.\""}},{"n":8,"text":"तमब्रवीत्ततो राजा प्रीयमाणः पुनः पुनः ।\nद्रोणकर्णादिभिः सार्धं पर्याप्तोऽहं द्विषद्वधे ।\nत्वं तु गच्छ मयाज्ञप्तो जहि युद्धं घटोत्कचम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The king, pleased again and again, said to him: \"I with Drona, Karna and the others am enough to kill the foe. But you, at my command, go and fight Ghatotkacha.\""}},{"n":9,"text":"तथेत्युक्त्वा महाकायः समाहूय घटोत्कचम् ।\nजटासुरिर्भैमसेनिं नानाशस्त्रैरवाकिरत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Saying \"So be it,\" the huge-bodied son of Jatasura, calling out to Ghatotkacha, showered Bhimasena's son with weapons of many kinds."}},{"n":10,"text":"अलंबलं च कर्णं च कुरुसैन्यं च दुस्तरम् ।\nहैडिम्बः प्रममाथैको महावातोऽम्बुदानिव ॥","meaning":{"en":"The son of Hidimba alone crushed Alambala, Karna and the hard-to-cross Kuru army, as a great wind scatters clouds."}},{"n":11,"text":"ततो मायामयं दृष्ट्वा रथं तूर्णमलंबलः ।\nघटोत्कचं शरव्रातैर्नानालिङ्गैः समार्दयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, seeing his illusory chariot, Alambala quickly struck Ghatotkacha with swarms of arrows of various marks."}},{"n":12,"text":"विद्ध्वा च बहुभिर्बाणैर्भैमसेनिमलंबलः ।\nव्यद्रावयच्छरव्रातैः पाण्डवानामनीकिनीम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having pierced Bhima's son with many arrows, Alambala drove the Pandava army to flight with those swarms of arrows."}},{"n":13,"text":"तेन विद्राव्यमाणानि पाण्डुसैन्यानि मारिष ।\nनिशीथे विप्रकीर्यन्त वातनुन्ना घना इव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Driven by him, the Pandava armies were scattered in the night, O king, like clouds blown by the wind."}},{"n":14,"text":"घटोत्कचशरैर्नुन्ना तथैव कुरुवाहिनी ।\nनिशीथे प्राद्रवद्राजन्नुत्सृज्योल्काः सहस्रशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"And likewise the Kuru army, struck by Ghatotkacha's arrows, fled in the night, O king, throwing away thousands of torches."}},{"n":15,"text":"अलंबलस्ततः क्रुद्धो भैमसेनिं महामृधे ।\nआजघ्ने निशितैर्बाणैस्तोत्त्रैरिव महाद्विपम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Alambala in a great rage struck Bhima's son in the great battle with sharp arrows, as one goads a great elephant with hooks."}},{"n":16,"text":"तिलशस्तस्य तद्यानं सूतं सर्वायुधानि च ।\nघटोत्कचः प्रचिच्छेद प्राणदच्चातिदारुणम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Ghatotkacha cut his chariot, charioteer and all his weapons into sesame-seed pieces, and then gave a most terrible shout."}},{"n":17,"text":"ततः कर्णं शरव्रातैः कुरूनन्यान्सहस्रशः ।\nअलंबलं चाभ्यवर्षन्मेघो मेरुमिवाचलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then he showered Karna, and thousands of other Kurus, and Alambala with swarms of arrows, as a cloud on the mountain Meru."}},{"n":18,"text":"ततः संचुक्षुभे सैन्यं कुरूणां राक्षसार्दितम् ।\nउपर्युपरि चान्योन्यं चतुरङ्गं ममर्द ह ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the Kuru army, tormented by the rakshasa, was thrown into turmoil and crushed its four divisions, one upon another."}},{"n":19,"text":"जटासुरिर्महाराज विरथो हतसारथिः ।\nघटोत्कचं रणे क्रुद्धो मुष्टिनाभ्यहनद्दृढम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The son of Jatasura, great king, chariotless and without a charioteer, in rage struck Ghatotkacha hard with his fist."}},{"n":20,"text":"मुष्टिनाभिहतस्तेन प्रचचाल घटोत्कचः ।\nक्षितिकम्पे यथा शैलः सवृक्षगणगुल्मवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Struck by his fist, Ghatotkacha shook, like a mountain with its trees and shrubs in an earthquake."}},{"n":21,"text":"ततः स परिघाभेन द्विट्संघघ्नेन बाहुना ।\nजटासुरिं भैमसेनिरवधीन्मुष्टिना भृशम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Bhima's son struck the son of Jatasura hard with his fist, with an arm like a bar, that kills throngs of enemies."}},{"n":22,"text":"तं प्रमथ्य ततः क्रुद्धस्तूर्णं हैडिम्बिराक्षिपत् ।\nदोर्भ्यामिन्द्रध्वजाभाभ्यां निष्पिपेष महीतले ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Hidimba's son, enraged, crushed him and quickly flung him down; with two arms like Indra's banners he ground him on the ground."}},{"n":23,"text":"अलंबलोऽपि विक्षिप्य समुत्क्षिप्य च राक्षसम् ।\nघटोत्कचं रणे रोषान्निष्पिपेष महीतले ॥","meaning":{"en":"Alambala, too, flinging up and hurling the rakshasa Ghatotkacha, in rage ground him into the ground in the battle."}},{"n":24,"text":"तयोः समभवद्युद्धं गर्जतोरतिकाययोः ।\nघटोत्कचालंबलयोस्तुमुलं लोमहर्षणम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"A fight arose between them, giant-bodied and roaring, Ghatotkacha and Alambala, tumultuous and hair-raising."}},{"n":25,"text":"विशेषयन्तावन्योन्यं मायाभिरतिमायिनौ ।\nयुयुधाते महावीर्याविन्द्रवैरोचनाविव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Each excelling the other with illusions, great illusionists, those two very mighty ones fought like Indra and Virochana's son (Bali)."}},{"n":26,"text":"पावकाम्बुनिधी भूत्वा पुनर्गरुडतक्षकौ ।\nपुनर्मेघमहावातौ पुनर्वज्रमहाचलौ ।\nपुनः कुञ्जरशार्दूलौ पुनः स्वर्भानुभास्करौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"They became fire and ocean, then Garuda and Takshaka; then cloud and great wind, then thunderbolt and great mountain; then elephant and tiger, then Rahu and the sun."}},{"n":27,"text":"एवं मायाशतसृजावन्योन्यवधकाङ्क्षिणौ ।\nभृशं चित्रमयुध्येतामलंबलघटोत्कचौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"So, creating hundreds of illusions, each wishing to kill the other, Alambala and Ghatotkacha fought in a most wonderful way."}},{"n":28,"text":"परिघैश्च गदाभिश्च प्रासमुद्गरपट्टिशैः ।\nमुसलैः पर्वताग्रैश्च तावन्योन्यं निजघ्नतुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"With iron clubs and maces, spears, hammers and battle-axes, with pestles and mountain peaks, they struck each other."}},{"n":29,"text":"हयाभ्यां च गजाभ्यां च पदातिरथिनौ पुनः ।\nयुयुधाते महामायौ राक्षसप्रवरौ युधि ॥","meaning":{"en":"On horses and on elephants, foot and in chariots by turns, those two great illusionists, best of rakshasas, fought in the battle."}},{"n":30,"text":"ततो घटोत्कचो राजन्नलंबलवधेप्सया ।\nउत्पपात भृशं क्रुद्धः श्येनवन्निपपात ह ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Ghatotkacha, O king, wishing to kill Alambala, leapt up in great anger and swooped down like a hawk."}},{"n":31,"text":"गृहीत्वा च महाकायं राक्षसेन्द्रमलंबलम् ।\nउद्यम्य न्यवधीद्भूमौ मयं विष्णुरिवाहवे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seizing the huge rakshasa lord Alambala, he raised and dashed him on the ground, as Vishnu did Maya in battle."}},{"n":32,"text":"ततो घटोत्कचः खड्गमुद्गृह्याद्भुतदर्शनम् ।\nचकर्त कायाद्धि शिरो भीमं विकृतदर्शनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Ghatotkacha, lifting a wonderful-looking sword, cut his terrible, distorted head from his body."}},{"n":33,"text":"तच्छिरो रुधिराभ्यक्तं गृह्य केशेषु राक्षसः ।\nघटोत्कचो ययावाशु दुर्योधनरथं प्रति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Taking that head, smeared with blood, by the hair, the rakshasa Ghatotkacha quickly went to Duryodhana's chariot."}},{"n":34,"text":"अभ्येत्य च महाबाहुः स्मयमानः स राक्षसः ।\nरथेऽस्य निक्षिप्य शिरो विकृताननमूर्धजम् ।\nप्राणदद्भैरवं नादं प्रावृषीव बलाहकः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Coming up, the mighty-armed rakshasa, smiling, threw the head with its distorted face and hair into his chariot, and gave a terrible roar like a cloud in the rains."}},{"n":35,"text":"अब्रवीच्च ततो राजन्दुर्योधनमिदं वचः ।\nएष ते निहतो बन्धुस्त्वया दृष्टोऽस्य विक्रमः ।\nपुनर्द्रष्टासि कर्णस्य निष्ठामेतां तथात्मनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, O king, he said this to Duryodhana: \"Here is your kinsman, killed; you have seen his prowess. You will see this same end for Karna and for yourself.\""}},{"n":36,"text":"एवमुक्त्वा ततः प्रायात्कर्णं प्रति जनेश्वर ।\nकिरञ्शरशतांस्तीक्ष्णान्विमुञ्चन्कर्णमूर्धनि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having said this, O lord of men, he went against Karna, scattering hundreds of sharp arrows and shooting them at Karna's head."}},{"n":37,"text":"ततः समभवद्युद्धं घोररूपं भयानकम् ।\nविस्मापनं महाराज नरराक्षसयोर्मृधे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then a terrible and fearful fight took place, wondrous, great king, between the man and the rakshasa in the battle."}}]}]}